  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protecting Vulnerable Migrants and Stabilizing Communities in Libya /Phase III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Over 10 years of political struggle in Libya have resulted in conflict, instability and community fragmentation with the country experiencing tremendous upheaval, considerably impacting people&apos;s lives in Libya. Foreign support to the conflict, military build-up, despite the embargo and armed clashes have led to massive displacement, damage to civilian infrastructures and loss of civilian lives. The erosion of the central authority and the armed clashes between different militias across the country have led to the displacement of hundreds of thousands of people, as well as damage to infrastructure and reduced access to basic services. Targeting migrants, internally displaced persons and vulnerable host community members across Libya, IOM aims to reinforce protection and resilience of migrants and host communities in Libya while supporting an improved migration management along migration routes in the country.</narrative>
  </description>
